    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Buyers looking for a city pad will be interested in this lovely property we are marketing in Ard Na Greine, Tycor.  Number 41 is a traditional two bedroom terraced house, in a mature, well established, neighbourhood close to the city centre.  This property features 56m2 of internal accommodation, gas fired central heating and secure off-street parking. \r\nThe ground floor accommodation features an entry hall, open plan living room with kitchen-diner, guest WC and Utility room/laundry.  Outside, there is a secure rear garden with a small timber shed. The first floor features two decent sized bedrooms and a shower room. \r\n\r\nThis property is conveniently located walking distance from the city centre. There are  three local bus routes close by (W1, W2 & W5) which will provide connections with the Cork Road, IDA industrial estate and SETU and The Quay in the city centre. Nearby schools include the Mercy schools, Presentation schools, Mount Sion, and De La Salle Stephen Street. \r\n\r\nLocal supermarkets include Aldi, Lidl, Supervalu (Hyper centre and/or Kilbarry). Mount Sion, Roanmore and De La Salle GAA clubs are nearby,\r\nOn big match days, hurling fans won't have far to walk to Walsh Park, only a few minutes away.\r\n\r\nThis house needs a little bit of cosmetic work to take it to its full potential, but can be a relatively easy project for a budding interior designer. \r\n\r\nCall or email us for viewing appointments. We look forward to seeing you."
      },
